Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 66/90] Mods' mobs animate smoothly; mods' first-person hands
 swing

The bridge draws a still or far mod mob every 2nd or 4th tick and keeps its look between; the game moved its pose from the look before to the new one within one tick and then held it: stepped, jerky animation (user: modded animals' animations look weird). Each look now records the ticks it stood (age) and the gap since the look before (span), and the pose moves over that whole gap. Positions move from last tick's place every tick, apart from the look. GeckoLib's custom meshes (most animated mod mobs) moved once a tick, vertex for vertex: they now move between the two looks as vanilla models' parts do.

The first-person capture passed 0 as the arm's swing: a hand a mod draws (Carry On's carry, guns, held models) stood still while vanilla's swung (user: the player's hand looks weird). It passes the player's swing on the swinging hand (LivingEntity.getSwingAnimation).

UMP: pack3 16/16; suite 77/77 before (far terrain patch).
